{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .refactor/critique-engine.md && git show e5a6605\"'^:docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md | sed -n '\"'112,120p'\"","aggregated_output":"# Plan critique: scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine.py\n\nReviewer: an Opus 5 critic run by the orchestrator with the refactor-python plan-critic instructions\n(the plugin's plan-critic agent exhausted its 20-turn cap on the 63 KB plan without a verdict; the cap\nis raised to 60 in the plugin source, commit d637cb2). Plan reviewed: `.refactor/plan-engine.md` as\nwritten by the split-planner (28 targets), then its revision.\n\n## Round 1 — REVISE (2026-09-17)\n\nBlocking:\n\n- **B1. Quoted `\"Engine\"` annotations in `_command_lock`.** `_peek_selected_chain` (engine.py:4362),\n  `_command_run_lock_id` (4383) and the inner `wrapped(self: \"Engine\", ...)` of\n  `_serialize_worktree_command` (4515) name `Engine` in string annotations; the inventory records only\n  `ast.Name` edges, so the plan copied the gap and ruff F821 would fail the wave gate. Fix: the same\n  `if TYPE_CHECKING: from forge_cli.engine._engine import Engine` guard `_finalize.py` gets, the\n  \"module does not exist yet\" type-baseline allowance from wave 2, Risk 5 grep expects two guards.\n- **B2. Trigger-table window (Risk 7).** After E2 no engine path matches the literal\n  `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine.py` in the `reviewer-routing` / `model-provider-version` rows. The\n  critic asked for the table change to precede E2. Rewritten as Option A (land first on main) and\n  Option B (accept the window; reintegration verification list). **Operator decision 2026-09-17:\n  Option B**, on the grounds that Forge is disabled on the branch, no gate evaluates there, and the\n  reintegration candidate both deletes `engine.py` and carries the repointed tables.\n- **B3. `plan-engine.json` wave 0 listed `state` and `core` side by side** although `core` references\n  `state`. Fix: `[state]`, `[core]`, then 17 / 6 / 2 / 1; prose states the orchestrator runs E0, E1,\n  E2 and the finalize wave by hand.\n\nAdvisory (round 1): `_ARCHIVE_MODULE` root re-export reads `None` after the split (nothing reads it;\nfollow-up bead); E0 accepted and flagged (62 sites, not ~70); E1 accepted and flagged — five fixtures\npatch `runtime.SCRIPT_DIR`, so a SCRIPT_DIR-based target is not value-identical under tests (confirmed\nby the E1 gate: `test_cli_merge_adapters` failed; E1 now resolves the shim from `runtime.__file__`);\nonly `_engine.py` (3,678 lines) is over budget; `external_dependents` in the inventory is empty but all\n222 moved names are re-exported; nothing beyond E0/E1 departs from a pure move.\n\n## Round 2 — APPROVE (2026-09-17)\n\nAll three fixes verified mechanically: guard present in the cluster, wave entry and Risk 5; no other\nquoted annotation exists (`grep -c '\"Engine\"'` = 3); 28 clusters, 223 symbols assigned once, no\nintra-wave edge, only backward edge `FinalizeContext -> Engine` (annotation-only); Option B's\nreintegration list is complete and executable. Advisory: state the exact site count (62 — applied);\nmake the JSON's scope explicit (the sentence under `## Waves` does); reword \"minus the one\n`TYPE_CHECKING` edge\" (applied).\n\nUnfinished: the final `__init__.py` code-line count is an estimate (measure in the finalize wave).\n- Plugin PostToolUse hook (`scripts/forge/invariant-guard.sh`) — advisory invariant feedback after Edit/Write\n- Plugin Stop/SessionStart hooks — the Stop union of telemetry aggregation plus a drift-staleness nudge, and the SessionStart drift-staleness nudge, in forge-initialized repos\n- `agents/review-final.md` — instruction-bounded, execution-capable Claude reviewer with a binding verdict; it has no Edit/Write tools but shares the orchestrator's writable worktree, so its no-write boundary is not an OS sandbox\n- `scripts/forge/{check-halt.sh,acquire-commit-lock.sh,release-commit-lock.sh,run-evals.sh,invariant-guard.sh,configure-dcg.sh,drift-check.sh,drift-staleness.sh,aggregate-telemetry.sh,commit-guard.sh,install.sh}` and `scripts/forge/{check-test-quality.py,archive-run.py,audit-commitments.py,emit-decision-event.py,journal-patterns.py}` — executable governance script surfaces\n- `scripts/forge/run-scoped-mutation.py` — Python-interpreter-loaded governance helper (the merge path invokes it as `python3 <path>` and the drift path imports it), so it is outside the executable-script inventory\n- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/` — the Python-interpreter-loaded package the Forge CLI is being split into (bead forge-plugin-95e): `scripts/forge/cli.py` remains the sole invoked entry point and shim that FR-221's matcher and the FR-223 corpora pin; the shim puts its own directory on `sys.path`, re-imports the envelope and policy names by explicit named lists, and forwards attribute reads of every `runtime`, `chain_core`, `engine`, and `app` `__all__` export through a module `__getattr__` (PEP 562), so every historical module attribute stays resolvable while tests reach the package through one shared loader (`tests/_cli_loader.py`); no file under it is executable, and it is outside the executable-script inventory exactly as `run-scoped-mutation.py` is. The package holds `envelope.py` (reason codes, `Refusal`, `FrozenError`, `Outcome`), `policy.py` (the committed-policy parser, whose fence helpers are the canonical patch seams), `runtime.py` (the one canonical module for the patchable controls — the clock, the bounded process runner, the merge lifecycle flag, the Revision-9 state controls, the path roots, the lazily imported coordination modules, the fast-tier mechanical-skip predicate, and the late-bound journal-record builder seam — which every module of the split reads by attribute so one in-memory patch on `forge_cli.runtime` disables a control everywhere), `candidate.py` (the shared bounded, pinned Git-context implementation for immutable tree snapshots, deterministic review evidence, marker identity, and raw produced-commit inspection), the `chain_core/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical module defined (its unused imports are not re-bound on the root), and whose modules — the root `__init__.py` and the submodules, together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the fenced process runner, the FR-235 common-lock arbiter and chain leases, chain and merge-chain storage, merge state and transition validation, the ingest verifiers, and the Revision-9 seam-marker loop (on the package root until bead forge-plugin-4j7 moves it beside `register_coordination_seams`)), `engine.py` (the commit-chain engine, argument-parser construction, finalize pipeline, review/approval/secret-scan helpers, archive surface, merge admission/scope/claim helpers, and Revision-12 bootstrap child protocol; it binds the journal-record builder onto the runtime seam at import), and `app.py` (`MergeEngine`, the shared chain-verb router, argument-parsing and dispatch entry points, and `main`; it obtains the parser and other engine helpers through `forge_cli.engine`). The existing FR-230 phase-3/4 manifest retains its historical production subjects; every changed or added production subject, including `candidate.py`, requires a current applicable Recorded-baseline integrity (`strict-evals`) result binding, plus `fresh-reviewer-evals` when the authenticated-base trigger matches; an unverifiable trigger blocks through its required INVALID path. The split changes no verb, diagnostic, reason code, `--help` byte, or immutable prior corpus.\n- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/fresh_evals.py` — the non-executable, Python-interpreter-loaded internal collector and verifier for candidate-bound fresh reviewer evaluation; behind the chain-owned `engine.py` launcher adapter it implements authenticated trigger derivation, candidate-tree fixture inventory and oracle withholding, bounded native child execution, canonical request-bound artifacts, manifest verification, and the current-candidate PASS predicate without adding a second CLI entry point\n- `scripts/forge/cli.py` — the Forge CLI commit-chain slice (FR-210..FR-224): a persisted chain state machine invoked as `python3 \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/forge/cli.py\" <verb>`, owning commit-chain sequencing, staging, candidate identity, evidence capture, and finalize. No PATH binary named `forge` is installed (the Foundry `forge` collision); `forge <verb>` anywhere in this spec is shorthand for that invocation form. Phase-gated: ships only after the FR-223 precondition evals pass\n- Phase-3 Forge CLI merge surfaces specified by FR-230..FR-237: `status`, `merge start|refresh|verify|gate run|approve|finalize|recover|cleanup|abort`, and the shared `review request|attach|disposition` verbs. These are normative future surfaces, not implementation delivered by Revision 7.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
