n    20\t\n     1\t## File & module size (enforced by tooling; see scripts/check_file_length.py, pyproject.toml)\n     2\t\n     3\t- No Python file over 500 code lines. If an edit would push a file over budget, STOP and\n     4\t  split it first with `/refactor-python:split-module <file>`, then make the change.\n     5\t- Files listed in `.refactor-baseline.json` are grandfathered: they may shrink, never grow.\n     6\t- Functions: complexity ≤ 10, ≤ 50 statements, ≤ 6 args (ruff C901 / PLR09xx). Existing\n     7\t  violations are listed per file under `[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]`; never add to\n     8\t  that list, and delete an entry when you clean or split its file.\n     9\t- Module boundaries are contracts in `[tool.importlinter]` (pyproject.toml); a new\n    10\t  cross-package import that breaks a contract is a design decision, not a fix. Raise it\n    11\t  instead of adding the import or an `ignore_imports` line.\n    12\t- Before finishing any task run:\n    13\t  `ruff check scripts tests system/fr223 && git ls-files -z \"*.py\" | xargs -0 python3 scripts/check_file_length.py && PYTHONPATH=scripts:scripts/forge lint-imports`\n    14\t  A failure is a blocker, not a warning. `pre-commit run --all-files` runs the same checks.\n    15\t- Refactor-only commits are prefixed `refactor(<area>):` and contain no behavior changes,\n    16\t  and still go through the Forge commit chain like every other commit.\n    17\t\n    18\t<!-- FORGE:BEGIN -->\ndiff --git a/.refactor-baseline.json b/.refactor-baseline.json\nindex df4ffeb..3b500e6 100644\n--- a/.refactor-baseline.json\n+++ b/.refactor-baseline.json\n@@ -8,15 +8,15 @@\n  \"scripts/forge/commitment_paths.py\": 659,\n  \"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app.py\": 11183,\n  \"scripts/forge/forge_cli/candidate.py\": 1195,\n- \"scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/__init__.py\": 665,\n+ \"scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/__init__.py\": 659,\n  \"scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/_activation.py\": 576,\n- \"scripts/fo